    # P_SCm - [SCm] PENETRATION FACTOR
    # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    # Definition: P_SCm = [SCm] penetration factor (dimensionless)
    #
    # CRITICAL: This is a PENETRATION factor, NOT a "presence" factor.
    # It quantifies how deeply [SCm] (Superconductive Material) penetrates
    # or interacts with a celestial body's interior.
    #
    # Physical Interpretation:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # [SCm] is a massless, extra-universal material present in all matter,
    # reacting with [UA] to build physical elements and drive universal dynamics.
    # P_SCm reflects how effectively [SCm] penetrates into the body's interior:
    #
    #   • Stars (plasma): P_SCm ≈ 1
    #     High conductivity allows magnetic fields and [SCm] interactions
    #     to permeate effectively throughout volume (core, convection, photosphere)
    #
    #   • Planets (solid/liquid): P_SCm ≈ 10⁻³
    #     Reduced penetration due to solid or liquid interior barriers,
    #     lower conductivity compared to stellar plasma
    #
    #   • Magnetars: P_SCm > 1
    #     Extreme magnetic field concentrations enhance [SCm] interaction
    #
    # Role in Universal Magnetism (Um):
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   Um = Σ_j[μ_j/r_j·(1-e^(-γt·cos(πt_n)))·φ̂_j]·P_SCm·E_react
    #        × (1 + 10¹³·f_Heaviside) × (1 + f_quasi)
    #
    # P_SCm directly scales the magnetic energy density, accounting for
    # how [SCm]'s interaction with magnetic strings affects the body.
    #
    # Example Um Scaling:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   Sun (P_SCm=1):      Um ≈ 2.28×10⁶⁵ J/m³
    #   Planet (P_SCm=10⁻³): Um ≈ 2.28×10⁶² J/m³ (1000× reduction)
    #
    # Relationship to P_core:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # P_SCm (penetration factor) and P_core (core penetration factor) are
    # related but distinct. Both reflect reduced penetration for planets,
    # with P_SCm affecting Um (magnetism) and P_core affecting Ug3 (rotation).
    #
    # Phenomena Affected:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   • Nebular dynamics: Magnetic string influence on dust/gas
    #   • Star formation: Collapse dynamics and jet formation
    #   • Quasar jets: Energy transfer from magnetic strings
    #   • Planetary magnetospheres: Reduced [SCm] influence
    #
    # ©2025 Daniel T. Murphy, daniel.murphy00@gmail.com – All Rights Reserved
    #
